{"id":"NCT07223944","title":"A Gaucher Disease Gene Therapy Trial With FLT201","official":"A Phase 3 Safety and Efficacy Trial of FLT201 Gene Therapy in Patients With Gaucher Disease Type 1","summary":"This study is a Phase 3, non-randomized, multicenter, efficacy and safety study in adult patients with Gaucher disease Type 1, on stable treatment with enzyme replacement therapy (ERT) or substrate reduction therapy (SRT) for at least 2 years. The study aims to confirm the efficacy and safety of FLT201 in this population after discontinuation of ERT/SRT.","conditions":["Gaucher Disease Type 1"],"interventions":[{"type":"GENETIC","name":"FLT201"}],"criteria":"Key Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Aged ≥18 years at time of screening.\n* Clinical diagnosis of Gaucher disease type 1\n* Stable hemoglobin concentration at baseline\n* Stable platelet count at baseline\n* Receiving ERT or SRT without interruption for at least 2 years\n\nKey Exclusion Criteria:\n\n* Diagnosed or suspected Gaucher disease type 2 or type 3\n* Positive for AAVS3 neutralizing antibodies.\n* Abnormal lab values, conditions or diseases that would make the participant unsuitable for the study\n* Positive pregnancy test or lactating\n* History of hematopoietic stem cell transplant (HSCT)/bone marrow transplant or any solid organ transplant.\n* History of receiving any gene therapy or cell therapy.\n* History of total splenectomy. Note: Additional protocol defined Inclusion and Exclusion criteria apply","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":45,"start":"2026-04-07","pcd":"2028-07-01","upd":"2026-10-14","sponsor":"Spur Therapeutics","areas":["other"],"central":["Spur Clinical Trials Contact · +44 (0)1438 906870 · clinicaltrials@spurtherapeutics.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Kaiser Permanente - CA","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90027","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":"Dr. Divya Vats · 626-646-4612 · divya.vats@kp.